```
Title: PowerShell Dynamic Module Invocation Via ExportedCommands Array Index - PS Script
Author: Norbert Jaśniewicz (AlphaSOC)
Date: 2026-10-06
Level: medium
Description: Detects obfuscated PowerShell scripts that enumerate Microsoft.PowerShell.Utility exported commands
 and invoke cmdlets indirectly by array index. This can be used to evade detections
 that look for explicit strings such as Invoke-RestMethod or Invoke-Expression.
MITRE Tactic: Execution
Tags: attack.execution, attack.stealth, attack.t1027, attack.t1059.001
Reference: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/windows/powershell/powershell_script/posh_ps_cmdlet_invocation_via_exported_commands_array_index.yml
 False Positives:
   - Legitimate use of exported commands array indexing in PowerShell scripts (should be rare)
```
ScriptBlockText="*[*]*" ScriptBlockText IN ("*Get-Module *", "*gmo *") ScriptBlockText="*ListAvailable*" ScriptBlockText="*Microsoft.PowerShell.Utility*" ScriptBlockText="*ExportedCommands*" ScriptBlockText="*Values*"